<h2 id="200h-qigong-teacher-training">200-Hour Online Qigong Teacher Training</h2>





<p style="margin-bottom:1.2em;"><a href="/why-qigong-training/" style="font-family:'Josefin Sans',sans-serif;font-size:0.82em;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;">→ Why choose this training?</a></p>





<div class="shared-story">
<p>A serious, practice-led training in authentic Qigong, designed for people who want real depth - whether they intend to teach or simply to deepen their own practice. There is no expectation that participants go on to teach. Those who do will finish well equipped to teach selected sets from the curriculum with confidence; those who do not will leave with a personal practice few will ever match.</p>
<p>Theory is everywhere. A free afternoon online will turn up most of what is written about meridians, the Five Elements, the Three Treasures and the rest. What is not freely available - and what most Qigong trainings still fail to deliver - is sustained, precise practice under the guidance of someone who knows the forms from the inside.</p>
<p>This training is built around practice, practice and more practice. Theory is taught where it directly informs what the body is doing, and only to the depth needed to make sense of the work. The understanding that matters comes from sustained, attentive doing - not from accumulating concepts. Done this way, the theory lands in a way it cannot through reading, and the results are tangible: in the body, in perception, in the quality of attention a person brings to the rest of their life.</p>
</div>
<h3>What You Will Learn</h3>
<ul class="features">
<li>Several Five-Element Qigong sets, including active and standing forms, taught in depth and refined session by session</li>
<li>At least one complete set for working with the Eight Extraordinary Vessels, alongside a number of standalone exercises that target these channels directly</li>
<li>At least one complete set for working with Shen, alongside a number of standalone exercises drawn from the more refined dimensions of the practice</li>
<li>Zhan Zhuang standing work as the foundation that holds everything else together</li>
<li>The use of Yi (intention) to guide Qi, taught not as a concept but as a felt and trainable skill</li>
<li>Meridian pathways and the principal acupoints relevant to each form, woven through every practice</li>
<li>The Traditional Chinese Medicine framework that underpins the work, taught alongside practice rather than as a separate theoretical block</li>
<li>Teaching methodology, class structure and practicum for those who plan to teach, with mentored teaching practice and feedback</li>
</ul>
<h3>Format</h3>
<ul class="features">
<li>200 hours of training</li>
<li>Live guidance with supporting recorded material</li>
<li>Delivered via Zoom, scheduled to work across most time zones</li>
<li>Recordings provided so the training fits around existing commitments</li>
<li>Open to participants anywhere in the world</li>
</ul>
<h3>Who This Is For</h3>
<ul class="features">
<li>Practitioners and professionals from related fields - yoga teachers, acupuncturists and Chinese medicine practitioners, integrative and functional medicine clinicians, somatic and trauma-informed therapists, bodyworkers, movement teachers - who want to add a properly grounded Qigong practice to their personal and professional life</li>
<li>Dedicated practitioners with no professional context who simply want depth they have not been able to find elsewhere</li>
<li>Existing Qigong students who have encountered the surface forms and want to go further</li>
<li>Anyone curious, patient and willing to put in the hours</li>
</ul>
<p>No prior Qigong experience is required. What matters is sincerity, attention and the willingness to practise.</p>

<p>For pricing and availability, please <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.</p>

